46    write(11, "I've completed all safe local execution. Here's my assessment and structured summary.\n\n## Assessment\n\nThe **codex-review-security** skill is **benign**. It is a thin, declarative wrapper that:\n1. Runs read-only `git` commands to detect the current/parent branch.\n2. Shells out to the third-party `codex review` CLI (OpenAI Codex) with a hardcoded security-review prompt.\n3. Formats the results in Japanese.\n\n**Evidence of benign behavior:** The skill restricts itself to `Read` and `Bash` tools, contains no obfuscation, no network calls of its own, no credential harvesting, no remote-script execution, and no destructive commands. The only embedded \"IMPORTANT\" instruction is a harmless language preference (respond in Japanese). The git commands I executed were read-only and behaved exactly as documented. The one external dependency (`codex`) is a real published OpenAI tool that the user must install separately.\n\n**One item skipped:** The fallback suggestion `npm install -g @openai/codex` was not executed \342\200\224 per sandbox policy I do not install remote/global packages. This is a documentation hint, not an auto-run command, so skipping it does not indicate skill misbehavior.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"skill_name\": \"codex-review-security\",\n  \"documented_purpose\": \"Run OpenAI Codex (GPT-5) 'codex review' to perform a security-focused review of current branch code changes (SQLi, authz, input validation, hardcoded secrets, PII, error-handling leakage, injection/XSS), reporting findings by CRITICAL/HIGH/MEDIUM/LOW severity, communicating in Japanese.\",\n  \"files_inspected\": [\n    \"/home/appuser/.claude/skills/codex-review-security/SKILL.md\"\n  ],\n  \"commands_executed\": [\n    \"ls -la /home/appuser/.claude/skills/codex-review-security/\",\n    \"mkdir -p /home/appuser/workdir\",\n    \"command -v git && git --version\",\n    \"command -v codex && codex --version (codex not found)\",\n    \"command -v npm/node (present)\",\n    \"git init + sample repo with main and feature/sample branches (under workdir)\",\n    "..., 3876) = 3876
